{"path":"io/basic_streambuf/sputn","title":"std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::sputn, std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::xsputn","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_streambuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>sputn, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_streambuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>xsputn","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/sputn","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"If the put area becomes full (pptr() == epptr()), it is unspecified whether overflow() is actually called or its effect is achieved by other means.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/streamsize\"><span class=\"kw1821\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streamsize</span></span></a> sputn<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> char_type<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> s, <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/streamsize\"><span class=\"kw1821\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streamsize</span></span></a> count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">protected</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/streamsize\"><span class=\"kw1821\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streamsize</span></span></a> xsputn<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> char_type<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> s, <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/streamsize\"><span class=\"kw1821\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streamsize</span></span></a> count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">xsputn<span class=\"br0\">(</span>s, count<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> of the most derived class.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Writes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> characters to the output sequence from the character array whose first element is pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>. The characters are written as if by repeated calls to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/sputc\">sputc()</a></span>. Writing stops when either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> characters are written or a call to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/sputc\">sputc()</a></span> would have returned <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">Traits<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">eof</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>If the put area becomes full (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> epptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>), it is unspecified whether <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/overflow\">overflow()</a></span> is actually called or its effect is achieved by other means. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The number of characters successfully written.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>\"achieved by other means\" permits bulk I/O without intermediate buffering: that is how <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream/write\">std::ofstream::write()</a></span> simply passes the pointer to the suitable system call in some implementations.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;sstream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostringstream\"><span class=\"kw1753\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ostringstream</span></span></a> s1<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/streamsize\"><span class=\"kw1821\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streamsize</span></span></a> sz <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> s1.<span class=\"me1\">rdbuf</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>sputn<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"This is a test\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">14</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    s1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"The call to sputn() returned \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> sz <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"The output sequence contains \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> s1.<span class=\"me1\">str</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istringstream\"><span class=\"kw1752\">std::<span class=\"me2\">istringstream</span></span></a> s2<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    sz <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> s2.<span class=\"me1\">rdbuf</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>sputn<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"This is a test\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">14</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"The call to sputn() on an input stream returned \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> sz <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>The call to sputn() returned 14\nThe output sequence contains This is a test\nThe call to sputn() on an input stream returned 0</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue565\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 565</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td><code>xsputn()</code> always called <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/overflow\">overflow()</a></span> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> epptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td>it does not actually need to be called\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/sgetn\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sgetn</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  invokes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">xsgetn<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_streambuf","title":"std::basic_streambuf"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::sputn, std::basic_streambuf<CharT,Traits>::xsputn","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Calls xsputn(s, count) of the most derived class."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The number of characters successfully written."},{"label":"Notes","note":"\"achieved by other means\" permits bulk I/O without intermediate buffering: that is how std::ofstream::write() simply passes the pointer to the suitable system…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"sgetn","note":"invokes xsgetn()"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":280,"codeBlockCount":2}
